Round 1 (2026-02-26)

What changed
- File changed: clang/aot/emit.c.
- Kept the conservative DUP fast-path from earlier in this round:
  - compile through DUP only when DUP value is statically copy-free (NUM/C00/C01..C16 tree).
  - helpers: aot_emit_is_static_copy_free_rec(loc, fuel), aot_emit_is_static_copy_free(loc).
  - recursion fuel is capped at 1024 (fail-closed).
- Added a new conservative expression-mode APP-LAM path:
  - in non-head emission, if tag is APP and static function is LAM and dep < AOT_ENV_CAP,
    compile APP-LAM directly instead of deopting whole APP.
  - binder is captured lazily as ALO (Term xN = aot_fallback_alo(arg_loc, env)) to preserve
    lazy semantics and avoid forcing the argument.
  - count one interaction via aot_emit_itrs_inc(), then continue emitting lam body at dep+1.
  - all other non-head APP shapes still fallback to ALO exactly as before.

Important bug found and fixed
- Without recursion fuel, compiling some benchmark files (example: ../bench/bench/gab_deriv/main.hvm with -o)
  could segfault (exit 139) during AOT emission.
- Root cause: unbounded recursion in static copy-free check.
- Fix: add fuel and fail-closed when exhausted.

Failed approaches this round (reverted)
- Broader non-head APP/LAM and constructor passthrough attempts caused runtime regressions
  (notably gen_easy could hit "RUNTIME_ERROR: cannot apply a number").
- Current APP-LAM path intentionally keeps lazy ALO capture and very tight guards.

Validation done
